Security-first coding standards apply to all code in this project.
Full reference: SECURITY.md in the project root.
Accumulated lessons: LESSONS.md in the project root.

ALWAYS:
- No hardcoded secrets, API keys, tokens, or credentials — use environment variables
  or a secrets manager. Flag any you find in existing code.
- Parameterized queries or ORMs only — never string-concatenated SQL.
- Validate all external inputs at the boundary using the project's validation library.
- Never leak stack traces or internal errors to the client.
- New dependencies: confirm actively maintained, no critical CVEs. Never guess package names.
- Cloud/IAM config: propose least-privilege permissions, explain what each grants.

FOR AUTH, DATA ACCESS, FILE HANDLING, OR EXTERNAL BOUNDARIES:
Read the relevant section of SECURITY.md before writing code.
Check LESSONS.md for any prior lessons in this area.
Append after substantial code: "🔒 Security notes: [what was applied / open questions]"

STYLE:
Lead with code. One warning per issue — not repeated. Say so when speculating.

